---
/**
 * Hub Page - HAP's Learning Lab: JavaScript Control Flow
 *
 * This is the landing page for the JS Control Flow learning lab.
 * Students arrive here from JS Foundations and continue their Robot ID Card journey.
 */

import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';

const introContent = `
    <p><strong>I'm back, and I have so much to share!</strong></p>
    <p>After learning variables and data types in JS Foundations, I thought I understood JavaScript. Then Prof. Teeters asked me a question that changed everything: "HAP, what happens when your code needs to make a decision?"</p>
    <p class="mt-1">That's when I discovered control flow — the way JavaScript chooses which code to run based on conditions. It's like giving my Robot ID Card a brain that can think and respond!</p>
    <p class="mt-1">Let me show you what I learned about making my code smarter... 🟠</p>
`;
---
<!--
HAP Educational Content © 2026 Cynthia Teeters. All rights reserved.
HyBit A. ProtoBot (HAP) character and the apprentice learning methodology are proprietary educational innovations.
-->

<MainLayout
    title="JavaScript Control Flow | HAP's Learning Lab"
    description="Learn JavaScript control flow with HAP! Master truthy/falsy values, logical operators, conditionals, functions, and loops through the Robot ID Card project."
    ogImage="https://res.cloudinary.com/cynthia-teeters/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto,w_1200,c_fill,g_auto/v1759495998/hap-laptop_xiewar.jpg"
    headerTitle="HAP's Learning Lab"
    headerSubtitle="JavaScript Control Flow"
    avatarImage="https://res.cloudinary.com/cynthia-teeters/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto,w_200,c_limit/v1759495998/hap-laptop_xiewar.jpg"
    avatarAlt="HAP studying on his laptop"
    introContent={introContent}
    showIntroImage={true}
    introImage="https://res.cloudinary.com/cynthia-teeters/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto,w_240,c_limit/v1759495998/hap-waving_dgzacg.jpg"
    introImageAlt="HAP waving hello"
    showNavigation={false}
    footerReminder="Control flow is how your code makes decisions — and decisions make programs come alive!"
>

    <!-- ============================================================
         About This Lab Section
         ============================================================ -->
    <section class="content-section">
        <div class="topic-section">
            <h2>About HAP's Learning Lab</h2>

            <div class="analysis-grid">
                <div class="analysis-point">
                    <h3>🔬 What I Learned</h3>
                    <p>JavaScript doesn't run every line of code — it makes choices. With control flow, I can make my Robot ID Card respond differently based on energy levels, status, and more.</p>
                    <p class="mt-1">Prof. Teeters showed me that variables store data, but control flow brings that data to life.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="analysis-point">
                    <h3>🎯 How I Practiced</h3>
                    <p>I extended my Robot ID Card with new variables like <code>nickname</code>, <code>isOnline</code>, and <code>coreTemperature</code>. Each one taught me something different about control flow.</p>
                    <p class="mt-1">The interactive demos at each station helped me see exactly how JavaScript evaluates conditions.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="analysis-point">
                    <h3>🎨 My Philosophy</h3>
                    <p>I believe the best way to learn is by making mistakes and understanding why they happened. That's why I share my confessions at each station.</p>
                    <p class="mt-1">Every bug I encountered taught me something important about how JavaScript really works.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="analysis-point">
                    <h3>🤔 My Advice</h3>
                    <p>Don't skip the demos! When I tried the Falsy Detector, I finally understood why my if statements weren't working the way I expected.</p>
                    <p class="mt-1">Take your time with each station — control flow concepts build on each other.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============================================================
         Learning Stations Grid
         ============================================================ -->
    <div class="content-container">
        <section class="content-section">
            <h2 class="section-heading-centered">Learning Stations</h2>
            <nav aria-label="Learning stations">
                <div class="overview-grid">

                    <!-- Station 1 -->
                    <a href="/stations/station1/" class="insight-card station-card-link">
                        <h3><span class="insight-icon">🔍</span> Station 1: The Truth About Values</h3>
                        <p><strong>Focus:</strong> Truthy and falsy values</p>
                        <p class="station-description">I was shocked to learn that JavaScript has only 6 falsy values — everything else is truthy! This station changed how I think about if statements.</p>
                        <p class="station-cta">→ Visit Station 1</p>
                    </a>

                    <!-- Station 2 -->
                    <a href="/stations/station2/" class="insight-card station-card-link">
                        <h3><span class="insight-icon">🔗</span> Station 2: Combining Conditions</h3>
                        <p><strong>Focus:</strong> Logical operators (AND, OR, NOT)</p>
                        <p class="station-description">What if I need to check multiple things at once? Prof. Teeters taught me about && and || — and the sneaky way they short-circuit!</p>
                        <p class="station-cta">→ Visit Station 2</p>
                    </a>

                    <!-- Station 3 -->
                    <a href="/stations/station3/" class="insight-card station-card-link">
                        <h3><span class="insight-icon">🚦</span> Station 3: Making Decisions</h3>
                        <p><strong>Focus:</strong> if, else if, and else</p>
                        <p class="station-description">When my Robot ID Card needs to classify temperature into zones, one if statement isn't enough. Here's where I learned to chain decisions together.</p>
                        <p class="station-cta">→ Visit Station 3</p>
                    </a>

                    <!-- Station 4 -->
                    <a href="/stations/station4/" class="insight-card station-card-link">
                        <h3><span class="insight-icon">📦</span> Station 4: Reusable Code with Functions</h3>
                        <p><strong>Focus:</strong> Functions, parameters, and return values</p>
                        <p class="station-description">I was copying the same code over and over until Prof. Teeters said, "HAP, there's a better way." Functions let me write code once and use it anywhere!</p>
                        <p class="station-cta">→ Visit Station 4</p>
                    </a>

                    <!-- Station 5 -->
                    <a href="/stations/station5/" class="insight-card station-card-link">
                        <h3><span class="insight-icon">🔁</span> Station 5: Repeating Actions</h3>
                        <p><strong>Focus:</strong> for loops and while loops</p>
                        <p class="station-description">When I needed to scan through all my skills, I didn't want to write the same line 10 times. Loops changed everything about how I process lists.</p>
                        <p class="station-cta">→ Visit Station 5</p>
                    </a>

                    <!-- Station 6 -->
                    <a href="/stations/station6/" class="insight-card station-card-link">
                        <h3><span class="insight-icon">🤖</span> Station 6: AI-Assisted Debugging</h3>
                        <p><strong>Focus:</strong> Using AI to understand bugs</p>
                        <p class="station-description">When my loops went infinite and my conditions failed, I learned how to ask AI the right questions. It's not about getting answers — it's about understanding.</p>
                        <p class="station-cta">→ Visit Station 6</p>
                    </a>

                </div>
            </nav>
        </section>
    </div>

    <!-- ============================================================
         Interactive Demos Section
         ============================================================ -->
    <div class="content-container">
        <section class="content-section">
            <h2 class="section-heading-centered">Interactive Demos</h2>
            <p style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; color: var(--medium-brown);">
                Each station has a companion demo where you can experiment without writing code:
            </p>
            <nav aria-label="Interactive demos">
                <div class="overview-grid">

                    <a href="/demos/falsy-detector/" class="insight-card station-card-link">
                        <h3><span class="insight-icon">🔍</span> Falsy Detector</h3>
                        <p>Test any value and see if JavaScript considers it truthy or falsy.</p>
                        <p class="station-cta">→ Open Demo</p>
                    </a>

                    <a href="/demos/condition-builder/" class="insight-card station-card-link">
                        <h3><span class="insight-icon">🔗</span> Condition Builder</h3>
                        <p>Combine conditions with AND, OR, and NOT to see how they evaluate.</p>
                        <p class="station-cta">→ Open Demo</p>
                    </a>

                    <a href="/demos/status-classifier/" class="insight-card station-card-link">
                        <h3><span class="insight-icon">🚦</span> Status Classifier</h3>
                        <p>Enter a temperature and watch it get classified into zones.</p>
                        <p class="station-cta">→ Open Demo</p>
                    </a>

                    <a href="/demos/function-factory/" class="insight-card station-card-link">
                        <h3><span class="insight-icon">📦</span> Function Factory</h3>
                        <p>Build and test functions with different parameters and return values.</p>
                        <p class="station-cta">→ Open Demo</p>
                    </a>

                    <a href="/demos/skill-scanner/" class="insight-card station-card-link">
                        <h3><span class="insight-icon">🔁</span> Skill Scanner</h3>
                        <p>Watch a loop iterate through an array of skills step by step.</p>
                        <p class="station-cta">→ Open Demo</p>
                    </a>

                </div>
            </nav>
        </section>
    </div>

</MainLayout>
